\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Likely biases\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 1. Outcome bias\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 You may judge a decision mainly by whether it worked, rather than by whether the process was fair, transparent, and repeatable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Countermeasure:
\f0\b0  Ask, \'93Would I defend this process if the outcome were poor?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 2. Control and influence bias\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 You may assume that deliberately shaping people\'92s choices is simply part of competent leadership. It often is, but the boundary between influence and manipulation can become unclear.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Countermeasure:
\f0\b0  Ask, \'93Does this person know what I am trying to influence, and can they disagree safely?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 3. Emotional underweighting\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Because you may tolerate stress or interpersonal discomfort relatively well, you might expect others to tolerate the same intensity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Countermeasure:
\f0\b0  Treat emotional impact as decision data, not as evidence of weakness.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 4. Moral licensing\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 Strong humility and ethical self-perception may unintentionally create the thought: \'93I am generally fair, so this exception is probably justified.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Countermeasure:
\f0\b0  Evaluate the specific action independently of your identity or prior record.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa327\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs32\fsmilli16380 \cf0 5. Competence-over-warmth bias\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs28 \cf0 You may give disproportionate weight to capability, delivery, intellectual quality, or strategic usefulness while underweighting trust-building and psychological safety.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Countermeasure:
\f0\b0  Assess both \'93what was delivered?\'94 and \'93what conditions did the person create for others?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

