\f1\b\fs56 \cf0 5. Short workplace scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\fs42 \cf0 Seeking feedback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Direct
\f0\b0 \
\'93I\'92m working on how I use authority under pressure. What is one thing I do that helps you speak candidly, and one thing that makes candour harder?\'94\

\f1\b Low-pressure
\f0\b0 \
\'93You don\'92t need to answer immediately. Thinking about our recent work, where did my style help, and where did it create unnecessary pressure?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Pausing before a reactive decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 In a meeting
\f0\b0 \
\'93I have a strong initial reaction, so I don\'92t want to confuse speed with judgment. Let me separate the facts from my assumptions before deciding.\'94\

\f1\b In writing
\f0\b0 \
\'93I\'92ve seen this and recognize that it needs a response. I\'92m going to pause before concluding anything, then come back with questions and next steps.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Giving credit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Public
\f0\b0 \
\'93The core insight came from [Name]. They identified [specific contribution], which changed how we approached the decision.\'94\

\f1\b When you developed the idea together
\f0\b0 \
\'93I helped shape the final version, but [Name] originated the key direction and deserves clear credit for it.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Repairing harm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Concise
\f0\b0 \
\'93I interrupted and dismissed your concern before understanding it. That made it harder for you to contribute. I\'92m sorry. Next time I will hear your full reasoning first. Is there anything I have missed about the impact?\'94\

\f1\b When the decision remains unchanged
\f0\b0 \
\'93I still believe the decision is necessary, but I handled the conversation poorly. The decision does not excuse the impact of my behaviour. I want to repair how we work together.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa348\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs42 \cf0 Responding to conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 De-escalating
\f0\b0 \
\'93Let\'92s slow this down. I want to understand what you believe is at stake before I defend my position.\'94\

\f1\b Firm but open
\f0\b0 \
\'93I disagree with that conclusion, but I do not want disagreement to become a contest. Let\'92s identify the facts we share, the assumptions we do not, and what evidence would resolve the difference.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa375\partightenfactor0

